トラベラーになれたら
and if only I could become a traveler.

343
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:46,847
俺ってやつはいつも気づいた時は手遅れ
A guy like me always realizes it when it's too late,

344
00:23:46,847 --> 00:23:50,047
絵空事ばかりうつつ抜かして
getting absorbed in nothing but pipe dreams,

345
00:23:50,047 --> 00:23:53,047
大事な人すら救えない
unable to save even the important people.

346
00:23:53,047 --> 00:23:56,547
だからこんな歌で自分に言い聞かせて
So with a song like this, I tell myself:

347
00:23:56,547 --> 00:24:00,047
あの時 あいつは多分気を使って
Back then, they were probably being considerate,

348
00:24:00,047 --> 00:24:03,247
とくに顔色かえず 何もないふり
not changing expression, pretending nothing happened.

349
00:24:03,247 --> 00:24:06,047
なんでいわないんだってムカついても
Even if I got annoyed, asking why they didn't say anything,

350
00:24:06,047 --> 00:24:09,847
やさしさからきてたなら しょうがないね
if it came from kindness, it can't be helped.

351
00:24:09,847 --> 00:24:15,047
願わくばディスコで親父と母さんが会った日に行きたいね
If possible, I'd like to go to the day my dad and mom met at the disco.

352
00:24:15,047 --> 00:24:21,047
後ろのジョックスに酒 かけて息子じきじきにチャンス作ってやるぜ
I'll spill a drink on the jocks behind them and personally make a chance for my dad.

353
00:24:21,047 --> 00:24:27,547
どんなでかい時計だってすべてさ 始まりはこんな小さい歯車
No matter how huge the clock, it all starts from a tiny gear like this.

354
00:24:27,547 --> 00:24:31,047
細かいことはもういいや 疲れた
Forget the petty details, I'm tired of it.

355
00:24:31,047 --> 00:24:35,047
別に怒ってないってさ 未来は
I'm not really angry, the future is...

356
00:24:46,047 --> 00:24:49,247
人はこれって時にどうしても
When people are in a pinch, no matter what,

357
00:24:49,247 --> 00:24:52,547
「時間を戻せたら」とかいうね
they say things like, "If only I could turn back time."

358
00:24:52,547 --> 00:24:56,247
でも誰も直せないよ 治せないんだな
But no one can fix it, no one can cure it.

359
00:24:56,247 --> 00:25:00,047
昔からそうだし まぁしょうがないね
It's been like that since way back, so it can't be helped.

360
00:25:00,095 --> 00:25:02,895
きっと先は深くて不安定
The road ahead is surely deep and unstable,

361
00:25:02,895 --> 00:25:06,695
でもお行儀よくちゃ つまんないね
but being well-behaved is no fun.

362
00:25:06,695 --> 00:25:08,895
タイムマシンに乗り込んで
If I hop into a time machine

363
00:25:08,895 --> 00:25:11,895
トラベラーになれたら
and become a traveler...

364
00:25:46,095 --> 00:25:51,095
Forever Young
[Song: Forever Young]

365
00:25:58,095 --> 00:26:03,095
シボレーのドアを蹴り開けて 街に飛び出した俺たち
Kicking open the Chevrolet door, we dashed out into the city.

366
00:26:03,095 --> 00:26:07,795
暴力 酒に女 音楽 中指立てる大人の仮面に
Violence, booze, women, music—flipping off the masks of adults.

367
00:26:07,795 --> 00:26:12,395
Oh さぁ踊ろう 「今日」という日を 生き急ぐメンバー
Oh, let's dance! Members living life in the fast lane today!

368
00:26:12,395 --> 00:26:17,095
足りねえか? Little louder! 欲望渦巻く路上が現場
Not enough? A little louder! The street swirling with desire is our scene!

369
00:26:17,095 --> 00:26:21,895
Yeah いつだってそうだろ ブルハ 尾崎 永ちゃんが教科書
Yeah, it's always been like that—Blue Hearts, Ozaki, E-chan were our textbooks.

370
00:26:21,895 --> 00:26:26,595
くたばるまで格好つけてぇ 誓ったよあの放課後
Wanting to look cool until we drop, we swore to it that day after school.

371
00:26:26,595 --> 00:26:31,095
俺らピーターパン 「またいつか」なんて言っちゃいかん
We're Peter Pans—don't go saying "maybe someday".

372
00:26:31,095 --> 00:26:35,895
嘲笑っとる大人に言ってやらぁ 人生はたったの一回だ
Tell those mocking adults: You only live once!

373
00:26:35,895 --> 00:26:40,895
胸の奥底 初期衝動
Deep within my chest, an initial impulse.

374
00:26:40,895 --> 00:26:45,095
見て見ぬフリ No, No
Pretending not to see, no, no!

375
00:26:45,095 --> 00:26:49,895
夢追い笑われ 傷だらけでギラつく My way
Laughed at for chasing dreams, covered in scars, glaring on my way!

376
00:26:49,895 --> 00:26:53,395
Go on! You should know who we are

377
00:26:53,395 --> 00:26:55,395
Forever Young

378
00:26:55,395 --> 00:27:00,095
Hey! Just next to me from now 大切なことは魂の状態
Hey! Just next to me from now. What matters is the state of your soul!

379
00:27:00,095 --> 00:27:04,095
Forever Young

380
00:27:04,095 --> 00:27:07,295
Hey! It's your turn next time from here

381
00:27:07,295 --> 00:27:09,595
「あの日始めれば良かった」
"I wish I had started back then."

382
00:27:09,595 --> 00:27:13,895
その次の始めるべき時は今
The next best time to start is right now!

383
00:27:13,895 --> 00:27:18,095
高笑いする都会の喧騒 ウケ狙いならば振り向けれんぞ
Loudly laughing urban clamor—if you're just fishing for laughs, I won't look back.

384
00:27:18,095 --> 00:27:23,095
何連呼? 忘れろ? 夢流した便所 見下ろしてきやがる摩天楼
Calling out what? Forget it? The toilet where dreams washed away, skyscrapers looking down on us.

385
00:27:23,095 --> 00:27:27,795
Oh まるで勝新みたく破天荒 伝説へとアテンド
Oh, unprecedented like Shintaro Katsu, attending us toward legend!

386
00:27:27,795 --> 00:27:30,095
怖にゃあ怖にゃあってその程度
Scared? Scared? Is that all you've got?

387
00:27:30,095 --> 00:27:32,495
捨てろ負け惜しみ 過去の栄光
Throw away sore excuses and past glory!

388
00:27:32,495 --> 00:27:36,195
永遠なんぞはねぇて いつか天へ召され
There's no such thing as forever; someday we'll be called to heaven.

389
00:27:36,195 --> 00:27:41,895
ペンで書き殴ったこの魂は 2PACみたく誰かの心を通過
This soul scribbled down with a pen, passing through someone's heart like 2Pac.

390
00:27:41,895 --> 00:27:46,295
なぁ 何か忘れちゃねぇか 人生まるで映画 皆がエンターテイナー
Hey, haven't you forgotten something? Life is like a movie, everyone's an entertainer!

391
00:27:46,295 --> 00:27:51,095
思い出せ 思想は現実化する 誰がHighway飛ばすBentayga
Remember, thoughts become reality! Who's speeding down the highway in a Bentayga?

392
00:27:51,095 --> 00:27:56,095
胸の奥底 初期衝動
Deep within my chest, an initial impulse.

393
00:27:56,095 --> 00:28:00,395
見て見ぬフリ No, No
Pretending not to see, no, no!

394
00:28:00,395 --> 00:28:05,095
夢追い笑われ 傷だらけでギラつく My way
Laughed at for chasing dreams, covered in scars, glaring on my way!

395
00:28:05,095 --> 00:28:08,595
Go on! You should know who we are

396
00:28:08,595 --> 00:28:10,595
Forever Young

397
00:28:10,595 --> 00:28:17,595
Hey! 俺達は今日だって 若気の至りのような夢を追いかけて来た
Hey! Even today, we've come chasing dreams born of youthful folly!

398
00:28:17,595 --> 00:28:20,095
Forever Young

399
00:28:20,095 --> 00:28:24,095
Hey! 変わるはずなんてない さぁ至ってやろうぜ!
Hey! There's no way we'd change! Come on, let's reach the peak!

400
00:28:24,095 --> 00:28:28,595
今日は残された人生で一番若い日だろ
Today is the youngest day left in your life, isn't it?

401
00:28:28,595 --> 00:28:32,595
半端な覚悟ならドブに捨てな (永遠)
Half-hearted resolve? Throw it in the gutter! (Forever)

402
00:28:32,595 --> 00:28:37,095
往生際が悪い テメー笑い飛ばし 誇れ Better days
Laugh off your bad sportsmanship and take pride in better days!

403
00:28:37,095 --> 00:28:41,895
まだ終わらない 終わらせやしない 燃え尽きるまで (永遠)
It's not over yet! Won't let it end until we burn out! (Forever)

404
00:28:41,895 --> 00:28:48,595
まだ終わらない 終わらせやしない くたばるまで (永遠)
It's not over yet! Won't let it end until we drop dead! (Forever)

405
00:28:48,595 --> 00:28:50,595
Forever Young

406
00:28:50,595 --> 00:28:57,895
もう夢を追いかけ本気になった心は 自分の指図も受けない
A heart that became serious about chasing dreams takes orders from no one, not even oneself!

407
00:28:57,895 --> 00:28:59,895
Forever Young

408
00:28:59,895 --> 00:29:08,895
Hey! その思いから逃れられないなら 自ら向かうだけ
Hey! If you can't escape those feelings, all you can do is head straight toward them!

409
00:29:08,895 --> 00:29:12,595
終わらせやしない 燃え尽きるまで (永遠)
Won't let it end until we burn out! (Forever)

410
00:29:12,595 --> 00:29:17,295
まだ終わらない 終わらせやしない くたばるまで (永遠)
It's not over yet! Won't let it end until we drop dead! (Forever)

411
00:29:17,295 --> 00:29:20,095
まだ終わらない まだ終わらない
It's not over yet! It's not over yet!

412
00:29:20,095 --> 00:29:22,095
Forever Young

413
00:29:22,095 --> 00:29:28,095
そう今日という日はお前に残された人生の一番若い日
Yeah, today is the youngest day left in your life!

414
00:29:36,095 --> 00:29:40,095
マリン！ 来てくれてありがとう！
Marine! Thank you for coming!

415
00:29:40,095 --> 00:29:43,095
ありがとう！
Thank you!

416
00:29:43,095 --> 00:29:48,895
いや マンジこの「Forever Young」って曲をマリンと一緒に歌いたかったの！
Seriously, I really wanted to sing "Forever Young" with you, Marine!

417
00:29:48,895 --> 00:29:52,095
あー、それはマリンがおばさんにならないように？
Ah, is that so Marine wouldn't become an old lady?

418
00:29:52,095 --> 00:29:55,295
そう！ もうForeverヤングなんだよっていうね！
Exactly! Telling you "You're Forever Young"!

419
00:29:55,295 --> 00:29:59,095
そうね、永遠にね！ ヤングな気持ちを... みんな Forever Young だよ！
That's right, forever! Keep a young heart... everyone is Forever Young!

420
00:30:00,070 --> 00:30:01,870
フォーエバーヤング！
Forever Young!

421
00:30:01,870 --> 00:30:05,070
で、マリン、今日はね、今日はね... 後ろ見て？
So Marine, today, you know... Look behind you!

422
00:30:05,270 --> 00:30:07,870
演奏してくれた...
They played the music for us...

423
00:30:08,070 --> 00:30:10,070
気まずいよ！
This is awkward!

424
00:30:10,070 --> 00:30:13,870
今日演奏してくれたみんなが乗ってるよ。どの人と写真撮りたい？
Everyone who played for us today is into it! Who do you want to take a photo with?

425
00:30:13,870 --> 00:30:17,870
え、そんな、1人だけみたいな... / 2人選んでいい、2人選んでいい！
Wait, picking just one person is... / You can pick two! You can pick two!

426
00:30:18,070 --> 00:30:20,870
かわいそうだから選ばれなかった... / 2人選ぼう、2人！
It'd be sad for whoever isn't picked... / Let's pick two! Two!

427
00:30:20,870 --> 00:30:24,070
ほら、もうコロネスキーが... / いや、マリンが選ぶんだよ。
Look, the Koroneskis are... / No, Marine is supposed to choose!

428
00:30:26,570 --> 00:30:30,070
じゃあ、最初は... / あ、待って！映して、後ろ。
So, first off... / Ah, wait! Show the back.

429
00:30:30,070 --> 00:30:34,070
みんな下向いて。
Everyone, look down.

430
00:30:38,570 --> 00:30:41,070
ホソイヌさん。
Hosoinu-san.

431
00:30:41,170 --> 00:30:43,870
かわいい！
So cute!

432
00:30:44,070 --> 00:30:47,370
じゃあ、まずホソイヌと写真撮ろうか。 / かわいいよ、ホソイヌ。
Okay, let's take a photo with Hosoinu first. / Hosoinu is so cute.

433
00:30:47,870 --> 00:30:51,070
こっちおいで、マリン。こっちね。 / はい、ホソイヌです。
Come over here, Marine. Right here. / Yes, this is Hosoinu.

434
00:30:51,170 --> 00:30:55,870
えっと、ホソイヌはギターかな？ギターですか？ホソイヌちゃん。
Um, Hosoinu plays guitar, right? Are you on guitar, Hosoinu-chan?

435
00:30:56,070 --> 00:30:58,370
ベロの色が... / かわいいね。 / 乾いてる、ベロ。
The color of his tongue... / It's cute. / His tongue is dry.

436
00:30:58,370 --> 00:31:03,070
ベロの赤、ちょっと澄んでるんだけど。 / あ、本当だ。乾いてるね。 / あんまり触らないでね。
His tongue is red... wait, it's a bit dull. / Ah, true. It is dry. / Don't touch it too much.

437
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:05,570
ごめんね、いっぱい触って。
Sorry for touching it so much.

438
00:31:05,670 --> 00:31:08,570
え、次誰がいい？ / あと1人、あと1人。
Who's next? / One more person, one more.

439
00:31:08,570 --> 00:31:11,170
じゃあ、フトイヌ？ / フトイヌ。 / フトイヌね。
Then, Futoinu? / Futoinu. / Futoinu, then.

440
00:31:11,270 --> 00:31:14,370
はい、フトイヌはドラムです！かわいいー！
Okay, Futoinu is on drums! So cute!

441
00:31:14,470 --> 00:31:17,070
でかい！
He's huge!

442
00:31:17,170 --> 00:31:19,070
かわいいね。
So cute.

443
00:31:19,170 --> 00:31:21,870
あ、ベロの色がちょっと明るい。
Ah, his tongue color is a bit brighter.

444
00:31:22,070 --> 00:31:24,070
ホソイヌより。
Than Hosoinu's.

445
00:31:24,170 --> 00:31:27,870
撮った？みんな撮ったー？ / 撮った！ / かわいいー！
Did you get it? Did everyone get the photo? / Got it! / So cute!

446
00:31:28,070 --> 00:31:30,170
オッケーだね。 / うん、オッケー。
All good then. / Yep, all good.

447
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:33,270
え、じゃあ最後さ、2人とも撮ろうよ、2人とも。 / あ、そうだね。2人とも撮ろう。
Hey, at the end, let's take one with both of us! / Ah, right. Let's take one with both of us.

448
00:31:33,870 --> 00:31:36,070
ごめん、キャプテン。
Sorry, Captain.

449
00:31:36,170 --> 00:31:38,270
え？
Huh?

450
00:31:38,870 --> 00:31:41,270
ちょっと...
Wait...

451
00:31:41,270 --> 00:31:45,070
あ、ごめんごめん！やっぱりとりで撮りたいみたいだから... / あ、やっぱりね。
Ah, sorry, sorry! Looks like they want to save the best for last after all... / Ah, of course.

452
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:47,870
コロネスキーともね、撮りますか。
Shall we take one with Koroneski too?

453
00:31:48,070 --> 00:31:52,570
コロネスキー、ころさん好き？好き？ころさん好き？
Koroneski, do you like Koro-san? Do you like her? Do you like Koro-san?

454
00:31:52,870 --> 00:31:55,870
あ、よかった。え、マリンも好き？ / 間に入ろう。
Ah, good. Wait, do you like Marine too? / I'll step in between.

455
00:31:56,070 --> 00:32:00,670
なんでさー！コロネスキーなのに、ころさんの隣に立てない気分どう？
Why?! How does it feel to be a Koroneski and not be able to stand next to Koro-san?

456
00:32:00,870 --> 00:32:03,570
嬉しい？マリンが隣で。
Are you happy that Marine is next to you?

457
00:32:03,670 --> 00:32:06,570
嬉しくない？本当は好きなんでしょ？
You're not happy? You actually like her, don't you?

458
00:32:06,570 --> 00:32:08,570
お前やめろよ！ / ダメ、もうダメ。帰るよ。
Cut it out! / No way, that's enough. I'm going back.

459
00:32:08,570 --> 00:32:11,170
帰るよ、もう。はい、帰ろう。
I'm going back. Okay, let me head back.

460
00:32:11,270 --> 00:32:14,270
はい、今日はね、バンドメンバーがいましたけれどもですね... / ええ。
Alright, today we had our band members with us, but... / Yeah.

461
00:32:14,370 --> 00:32:17,370
はい。え、マリンとも最後撮りたい！ / あ、撮ろう撮ろう！せっかくね。
Yep. Ah, I want to take a photo with Marine at the end too! / Ah, let's do it! Since we're here.

462
00:32:17,470 --> 00:32:20,570
Forever Youngだから、今日は。
Because today is 'Forever Young'.

463
00:32:20,670 --> 00:32:24,070
マイク... マイク間違っちゃってるけどさ。
Microphone... Your mic is facing the wrong way, though.

464
00:32:24,170 --> 00:32:27,370
マイクね。うん、いいよいいよ。
The mic, yeah. Yeah, it's fine, it's fine.

465
00:32:27,470 --> 00:32:30,870
でかい声で喋れば拾うから！
As long as you speak loudly, it'll pick it up!

466
00:32:30,970 --> 00:32:33,170
撮れたー？
Did you get it?

467
00:32:33,270 --> 00:32:35,870
いけてる？ / フトイヌ...
Is it good? / Futoinu...

468
00:32:35,870 --> 00:32:38,270
中心として... / いい顔撮れたね。
As the center... / Got a great face captured!

469
00:32:38,370 --> 00:32:40,570
ありがとう、マリン！ / ありがとう！
Thank you, Marine! / Thank you!

470
00:32:40,670 --> 00:32:43,670
これね、ちょっと次の曲があるから行くけど... / あ、次の曲。
Well, I have the next song coming up, so I have to go, but... / Ah, the next song.

471
00:32:43,670 --> 00:32:46,570
1人で帰れる？ / お、え、え、そんな... あ、うん、大丈夫。大丈夫大丈夫。
Can you head back by yourself? / Oh, wait... Ah, yeah, I'm fine. I'm fine, I'm fine.

472
00:32:46,670 --> 00:32:49,070
じゃあ、バンドメンバーのことよろしく。 / え？
Alright, take care of the band members for me! / Huh?

473
00:32:49,170 --> 00:32:51,570
じゃあマリン、バイバーイ！ / え、よろしくって何によろしく...
Bye-bye, Marine! / Wait, what do you mean take care of them...

474
00:32:52,570 --> 00:32:56,070
どんなムードこれ... あ、え？
What kind of mood is this... Ah, wait?

475
00:32:56,070 --> 00:32:58,870
あ、みんな... あ、あえ？そしてみんな！次の曲だよ！
Ah, everyone... Ah, wait? And everyone, it's time for the next song!

476
00:33:00,570 --> 00:33:05,070
のびしろ
Room to grow...

477
00:33:07,570 --> 00:33:13,270
サボり方とか 甘え方とか 逃げ方とか 言い訳の仕方とか
Knowing how to slack off, how to depend on others, how to run away, how to make excuses...

478
00:33:13,270 --> 00:33:19,070
やっと覚えて来た 身につけて来た 柔らかい頭
I've finally learned it, acquired it—a flexible mind.

479
00:33:19,070 --> 00:33:24,570
カッコのつけ方 調子のこき方 腹の据え方 良い年のこき方
How to look cool, how to get carried away, how to brace myself, how to act my age...

480
00:33:24,570 --> 00:33:30,070
脂乗りに乗った 濁った目した だらしナイ身体
In my prime, with cloudy eyes, and a sloppy body.

481
00:33:30,070 --> 00:33:35,570
嫌われ方や 慕われ方や 叱り方とか 綺麗なぶつかり方
How to be hated, how to be liked, how to scold, and how to clash gracefully...

482
00:33:35,570 --> 00:33:40,070
もっと覚えたい事が山のようにある
There are still mountains of things I want to learn.

483
00:33:40,070 --> 00:33:41,570
のびしろしかないわ
I've got nothing but room to grow.

484
00:33:41,570 --> 00:33:43,070
のびしろしかないわ
I've got nothing but room to grow.

485
00:33:43,070 --> 00:33:45,070
のびしろしかないわ
I've got nothing but room to grow.

486
00:33:45,070 --> 00:33:49,070
のびしろしかないわ
I've got nothing but room to grow.

487
00:33:49,070 --> 00:33:52,070
俺らまだのびしろしかないわ
We've still got nothing but room to grow.

488
00:33:52,070 --> 00:33:55,070
悪者扱いして来た街で
In the town that treated me like a villain,

489
00:33:55,070 --> 00:33:57,870
悪者扱いして来たオトナへ
To the adults who treated me like a villain,

490
00:33:57,870 --> 00:34:00,870
変わりゆく俺 鏡の中へ
My changing self, into the mirror,

491
00:34:00,870 --> 00:34:03,270
尋ねても答えない yeah yeah yeah
Even if I ask, it won't answer, yeah yeah yeah.

492
00:34:03,270 --> 00:34:05,870
去る者は追わない 引くとこ引いて
I don't chase those who leave, pulling back when I should,

493
00:34:05,870 --> 00:34:08,570
丸く収めたり 軽くいなして
Smoothing things over or lightly parrying,

494
00:34:08,570 --> 00:34:11,270
鏡の中でわろてるお前
You, laughing in the mirror,

495
00:34:11,270 --> 00:34:14,270
括れやしなかったたったの三文字で
Couldn't be bound by just three simple words.

496
00:34:14,270 --> 00:34:17,070
日々重くなる足取りで
With footsteps growing heavier every day,

497
00:34:17,070 --> 00:34:20,070
自分の歩幅で闊歩してる
Stride along at your own pace.

498
00:34:20,070 --> 00:34:22,570
カマすとこカマす まかすとこまかす
Show off where you show off, leave things where you leave them,

499
00:34:22,570 --> 00:34:25,270
割と適当な段取りで
With a fairly casual plan,

500
00:34:25,270 --> 00:34:28,070
やっと分かって来たかも
Maybe I've finally figured out

501
00:34:28,070 --> 00:34:30,870
このポンコツの操縦の仕方
How to control this piece of junk.

502
00:34:30,870 --> 00:34:33,570
19の時の「ついに来たか」より
More than the "It's finally here" back when I was 19,

503
00:34:33,570 --> 00:34:36,570
もっと清々しい気持ち
A much more refreshing feeling,

504
00:34:36,570 --> 00:34:38,270
隅田川にかかる
Spanning over the Sumida River,

505
00:34:38,270 --> 00:34:41,070
勝鬨橋を渡る
Crossing the Kachidoki Bridge,

506
00:34:41,070 --> 00:34:43,570
左手にスカイツリー
Skytree on my left hand,

507
00:34:43,570 --> 00:34:46,570
右手に東京タワー 俺はその真ん中
Tokyo Tower on my right hand, and I'm right in the middle.

508
00:34:46,870 --> 00:34:52,570
サボり方とか 甘え方とか 逃げ方とか 言い訳の仕方とか
Knowing how to slack off, how to depend on others, how to run away, how to make excuses...

509
00:34:52,570 --> 00:34:58,070
やっと覚えて来た 身につけて来た 柔らかい頭
I've finally learned it, acquired it—a flexible mind.

510
00:34:58,070 --> 00:35:01,070
カッコのつけ方 調子のこき方...
How to look cool, how to get carried away...

511
00:35:00,118 --> 00:35:04,018
カッコのつけ方 調子のこき方 腹の据え方 良い年のこき方
How to act cool, how to get carried away, how to settle down, how to age gracefully,

512
00:35:04,118 --> 00:35:08,918
脂の乗った 濁った目をした だらし無かった
In my prime, with muddy eyes, I was so sloppy.

513
00:35:09,618 --> 00:35:12,918
幸せの体感速度は
The perceived speed of happiness...

514
00:35:13,118 --> 00:35:15,118
早く良くなるばかり
...only keeps getting faster.

515
00:35:15,518 --> 00:35:18,118
傷が癒えていく速度は
The speed at which wounds heal...

516
00:35:18,318 --> 00:35:20,618
遅くなるばかり
...only keeps getting slower.

517
00:35:21,118 --> 00:35:26,118
他人に期待をしないのが 今の俺の強み
Not expecting anything from others is my strength now.

518
00:35:26,618 --> 00:35:29,918
手負いでも進める距離なら
If it's a distance I can cover even when wounded...

519
00:35:30,318 --> 00:35:33,918
伊達や猥雑 身の程を知るほどに
Knowing my limits all the more,

520
00:35:33,918 --> 00:35:36,618
胸を張り いつも通り
Pushing out my chest, just like always,

521
00:35:36,618 --> 00:35:39,318
でも時にしたたかに背伸び
But sometimes slyly stretching beyond my reach,

522
00:35:39,318 --> 00:35:42,318
やっと「大人気ない」ができる歳
Finally at an age where I can be "immature",

523
00:35:42,318 --> 00:35:46,118
小さな枠組み ただの数字 縛られずに
Unbound by small frameworks or mere numbers.

524
00:35:46,118 --> 00:35:49,918
でも腹くくり あの日の俺が立ち止まる
But bracing myself, the me from that day comes to a halt...

525
00:35:49,918 --> 00:35:53,318
ほどにデカくそびえ立つ
...in front of something towering so huge,

526
00:35:53,318 --> 00:35:57,918
隅田川にかかる 勝鬨橋を渡る
Crossing Kachidoki Bridge over the Sumida River.

527
00:35:58,118 --> 00:36:01,118
重なるスカイツリー
Overlapping Tokyo Skytree,

528
00:36:01,118 --> 00:36:04,318
東京タワーと真ん中の頼りない背中
And Tokyo Tower, with a slender back right in between.

529
00:36:04,318 --> 00:36:09,918
サボり方とか 甘え方とか 逃げ方とか言い訳の仕方とか
How to slack off, how to depend on others, how to run away, how to make excuses...

530
00:36:09,918 --> 00:36:15,118
やっと覚えて来た 身につけて来た 柔らかい頭
I've finally learned, acquired a flexible mind.

531
00:36:15,318 --> 00:36:21,118
カッコのつけ方 調子のこき方 腹の据え方 良い年のこき方
How to act cool, how to get carried away, how to settle down, how to age gracefully,

532
00:36:21,118 --> 00:36:25,918
脂の乗った 濁った目をした だらし無かった
In my prime, with muddy eyes, I was so sloppy.

533
00:36:26,318 --> 00:36:32,918
嫌われ方や 慕われ方や 叱り方とか 綺麗なぶつかり方
How to be hated, how to be loved, how to scold, how to clash gracefully...

534
00:36:32,918 --> 00:36:36,118
覚えた事が山のようにある
I have a mountain of things I've learned.

535
00:36:36,118 --> 00:36:44,318
のびしろしか無いわ
There's nothing but room to grow!

536
00:36:44,618 --> 00:36:50,118
俺達まだのびしろしかないわ
We still have nothing but room to grow!

537
00:36:55,618 --> 00:36:58,618
くだんない話と
Silly conversations,

538
00:36:58,618 --> 00:37:01,318
うざったい貴様と
and an annoying fellow like you,

539
00:37:01,318 --> 00:37:04,318
なみなみの日々に 注がれてく
Being poured into ordinary days,

540
00:37:04,318 --> 00:37:07,118
怠いが溢れ出していく
A sense of sluggishness overflows.

541
00:37:07,118 --> 00:37:09,618
飯がまだ届かない
The food hasn't arrived yet,

542
00:37:09,618 --> 00:37:12,118
仕事は片付かない
Work isn't getting finished,

543
00:37:12,118 --> 00:37:17,118
うだつの上がらない 毎日にため息ばかり
Sighing every day in an unproductive life.

544
00:37:17,318 --> 00:37:19,618
でまたド派手にすっころび
And then taking a spectacular fall again,

545
00:37:19,618 --> 00:37:21,918
洗い立てのシャツにこぼすコーヒー
Spilling coffee on a freshly washed shirt,

546
00:37:21,918 --> 00:37:24,118
前のめり その姿勢だけは褒めて良し
Leaning forward—at least praise that attitude!

547
00:37:24,118 --> 00:37:26,918
肩落とす並木通り 増えた柄と差し色に
Walking down the tree-lined avenue with slumped shoulders, with added patterns and accent colors.

548
00:37:26,918 --> 00:37:29,918
嗚呼…本当嫌なる毎日だ
Ah... these days are truly depressing.

549
00:37:29,918 --> 00:37:32,318
やりたくないことやったって
Even if I do things I don't want to do,

550
00:37:32,318 --> 00:37:34,618
嫌々早起きしたって
Even if I reluctantly wake up early,

551
00:37:34,618 --> 00:37:39,918
その分素敵な何かが 訪れるとかそんなわけでもないのにさ
It doesn't mean something wonderful will come my way, and yet...

552
00:37:40,118 --> 00:37:42,618
今日にもまた頑張っちゃうよな
Here I am trying hard again today.

553
00:37:42,618 --> 00:37:45,118
がむしゃら以外知らないから
Because I don't know any other way than reckless effort.

554
00:37:45,118 --> 00:37:51,118
不器用で意地張りで 馬鹿真面目な僕らに幸あれ
May happiness come to us clumsy, stubborn, stupidly honest ones.

555
00:37:52,118 --> 00:37:56,118
重くなってきた荷物をちょっと置いて立ち止まり
Setting down the heavy luggage for a moment to pause,

556
00:37:56,118 --> 00:37:58,618
昨日の事なんぞ忘れちまえば同じ
Forgetting yesterday's troubles makes no difference anyway.

557
00:37:58,618 --> 00:38:00,918
浴びるdaylight 羽根伸ばし
Basking in the daylight, stretching my wings,

558
00:38:00,918 --> 00:38:03,618
それか月夜にこっそりと吐き出してしまえば良い
Or secretly venting it all out under the moonlit night.

559
00:38:03,618 --> 00:38:06,118
でもその前にアレとコレの話
But before that, let's talk about this and that.

560
00:38:06,118 --> 00:38:08,618
その為にはまずはソレを片して
For that to happen, first clean that up!

561
00:38:08,618 --> 00:38:10,918
っで今何時？ いやその前に
Wait, what time is it now? No, before that...

562
00:38:10,918 --> 00:38:13,618
今日もなんだかんだ騒がしい毎度あり
Today is noisy one way or another again, thanks as always!

563
00:38:13,918 --> 00:38:18,118
1ヶ月くらい何にも 考えずだらだらしていたいな
I want to laze around for about a month without thinking of anything,

564
00:38:18,118 --> 00:38:22,118
ゆっくり休んで遊んで眠っていたいな
Rest comfortably, play, and just sleep...

565
00:38:22,118 --> 00:38:25,118
って思う日もあるけれど
There are days when I think like that, but...

566
00:38:25,318 --> 00:38:27,918
やっとここまで来たんだよ
We've finally made it this far,

567
00:38:27,918 --> 00:38:30,318
ここじゃ終われないんだよ
We can't end it here!

568
00:38:30,318 --> 00:38:35,118
辛いきついもいつかは 笑い話にできると信じてるんだほら
Believing that all the pain and hardship will become a laughing matter someday, see?

569
00:38:35,318 --> 00:38:37,918
今日もまた頑張っちゃうからさ
I'll work hard again today,

570
00:38:37,918 --> 00:38:40,318
がむしゃらに愛を歌うからさ
Sing love recklessly!

571
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:43,118
目一杯吸い込んだ空気
Taking a deep breath of air,

572
00:38:43,318 --> 00:38:46,118
嗚呼 本当素晴らしい毎日だ
Ah, what a truly wonderful everyday life!

573
00:38:46,118 --> 00:38:48,618
やりたくないことやったって
Even if I do things I don't want to do,

574
00:38:48,618 --> 00:38:51,118
嫌々早起きしたって
Even if I reluctantly wake up early,

575
00:38:51,118 --> 00:38:53,118
ほんの少しの幸せに
Just touching a tiny bit of happiness...

576
00:38:53,118 --> 00:38:56,118
触れるだけで全部全部ありに思えるんだ
...makes everything feel totally worth it!

577
00:38:56,118 --> 00:38:58,618
明日もまた頑張ってみようか
Shall we try our best again tomorrow?

578
00:38:58,618 --> 00:39:01,118
がむしゃらに生きていくんだ
Living recklessly forward!

579
00:39:01,118 --> 00:39:06,918
不器用で意地張りで 馬鹿真面目な僕らに幸あれ
May happiness come to us clumsy, stubborn, stupidly honest ones.

580
00:39:06,918 --> 00:39:11,918
do my thing do your thing 肩の力を抜いて柔軟に
Do my thing, do your thing, relax your shoulders and stay flexible.

581
00:39:11,918 --> 00:39:17,318
again do my thing do your thing あと1ミリ背伸び
Again, do my thing, do your thing, stretching just 1mm further.

582
00:39:17,318 --> 00:39:20,118
嗚呼 本当嫌になっちゃうよな
Ah, it truly gets frustrating, doesn't it?

583
00:39:20,118 --> 00:39:22,318
それでも今を生きている
Even so, we live in the present.

584
00:39:22,318 --> 00:39:28,118
不器用で意地張りで 馬鹿真面目なあなたに幸あれ
May happiness come to you, clumsy, stubborn, and stupidly honest.

585
00:40:12,793 --> 00:40:17,893
リーズナブルな完成度＋スケスケまくりのimitation
A reasonable level of completion + a transparent imitation

586
